Design Log - Late Work Management System
Entry 1 — Dashboard Layout & Visual Hierarchy
Design Issue
The original interface made it difficult for Mr Marshall to quickly identify which students had missing or late work. All assignments were displayed with equal visual weight, causing confusion and slow decision-making.
Design Principles Applied
•	Hierarchy
•	Alignment
•	Contrast
UX Characteristics
•	Usability
•	Efficiency
Design Change
I redesigned the dashboard so that:
•	“Missing Work” appears at the top in a bold section
•	“Late” and “Submitted” items are separated into clear columns
•	Important alerts (missing submissions) are highlighted with stronger contrast
Before, all entries looked identical. After the change, critical tasks visually stand out first.
Impact on User Experience
Mr Marshall can now immediately identify urgent tasks without scanning the entire list. This improves efficiency and usability, especially during busy marking periods.
